Package: psf-security-packages
Version: @FULL@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINT@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: bash (>= 4.0)
Suggests: apparmor-utils, auditd
Homepage: https://codeberg.org/PrivacySafe/security-patches
Description: PrivacySafe security checks, hunts and interim mitigations
 Free public domain tools for GNU/Linux servers: check whether you are
 exposed, hunt for signs of exploitation, and apply interim mitigations where
 the vendor fix is not enough. Covers PHP2Shell (CVE-2026-109618 and
 CVE-2026-109619), Nextcloud Collabora, nginx, curl, Brotli, libheif, Ruby
 and GitLab, Plex, LiteLLM, GhostAction and more.
 .
 Everything installs under /opt/psf-security-patches, plus the
 php2shell-watch systemd unit, which is not enabled automatically. Patching
 is the fix: these tools reduce risk while you patch and help you find out
 whether you were hit.
 .
 Built and published by PrivacySafe Foundation 501(c)(3) nonprofit with the
 assistance of Ivy Cyber LLC. CC0 1.0 Universal.
